00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.779
So if I submit a hotfix, for example, or a bugfix,

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.200
how do you decide what goes into which release?

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:28.340
So we have different types of release. So right

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:31.899
now, the main branch is for Python 3 .15, which

00:12:31.899 --> 00:12:34.159
will be released in October next year. So all

00:12:34.159 --> 00:12:36.480
new features go into that. And we'll start doing

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:40.209
alpha releases for that in May next year. And

00:12:40.209 --> 00:12:43.090
right now we have 3 .14 is the forthcoming one.

00:12:43.809 --> 00:12:46.710
So no more features are allowed in there. The

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:51.909
cutoff for that was in May as well. And so there

00:12:51.909 --> 00:12:55.110
we only have bug fixes coming now, which will

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:58.629
